* Simple 'scripts' -- more like batch files for stuff that would have been typed into chat box --
  - see /exec -e which runs a command and interprets as a batch / chat input (parse / and ! commands); 
    - maybe /exec -e !file | !"file" syntax? or maybe -c for cat?
  - This would let us setup our quick tasks like:
    ON CONNECT rplywv00 EXEC -c scripts/rplywv00.connect
    ON CONNECT rplywv00.rig0 EXEC -c scripts/rplywv00.rig0.connect
 
  Those scripts can contain anything the user could input at the chat input prompt presently
  The functionality already exists mostly in /exec -e to run another process, we would make -c just read a file
